<title>ITALY: Italian CPI 1.4 pct in June -Istat.</title>
<headline>Italian CPI 1.4 pct in June -Istat.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Statistics Office</p>
<p>(ISTAT) reported the following consumer inflation details:</p>
<p> ITALIAN INFLATION	   June 97    May 97	June 96</p>
<p> Monthly CPI index rise	 0.0	  0.3	  0.2</p>
<p> Yr-on-yr inflation	     1.4	  1.6	  3.9</p>
<p> Index (Base 1996)	    105.7	105.7	104.2</p>
<p>Istat said that including tobacco costs in the inflation data gave a CPI rate of 1.5 percent for June.  </p>
<p>ISTAT gave the following sector-by-sector breakdown.</p>
<p> Sector			   Index	   mo/mo (%)    yr/yr (%)</p>
<p> Food (without tabacco)     104.2	   +0.1	   -0.9</p>
<p> Clothing			 106.8	   +0.1	   +2.5</p>
<p> Housing,Electricity,Fuel   109.3	   -0.1	   +4.0</p>
<p> Domestic goods		 105.4	    0.0	   +1.4</p>
<p> Health spending		105.9	   +0.2	   +3.0</p>
<p> Transport			106.3	   +0.1	   +1.5</p>
<p> Recreation		     103.0	   -0.4	   +0.1</p>
<p> Education			107.5	    0.0	   +3.4</p>
<p> Hotels, restaurants	  106.6	   +0.2	   +2.3</p>
<p> Other goods,services	 105.2	   +0.1	   +2.1</p>
<p>--Rome newsroom 396-6782501</p>
</text>
